{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Teach me</b> — accustom me, in the sense of: a wild ass accustomed to the desert." "And some say: that he likened himself to being in the midst of the sea, therefore he asks for a good spirit that will lead him out to land. Or, a bet may be missing, and it is: הישר בעיניך ברוחך טובה תנחני (what is upright in Your eyes, in Your good spirit You will lead me), and the tav is for the direction of HaShem. And R. Solomon the Spaniard, of blessed memory, said: the power of the supernal spirit."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 143, :notes {1 "The phrase 'the tav is for the direction of HaShem' translates לנכח השם hyper-literally; the exact grammatical point Ibn Ezra intends by this is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:38.304754904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}